      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LAST AFFAIR (5) went fairly on debut over 1300m at Illawarra Grange then was ridden closer to the pace and got the cash last Saturday over 1500m at Newcastle. Coming along nicely and is bred to want ground so this slightly longer trip suits. The one to beat again. MAYLEIGH (4) gave away a big start in the early stages but went through her gears nicely to record a maiden win over 1400m at this track recently. Strips fitter and an extra 200m is a positive progression. CAP D'AIL (1) looked in need of a longer trip last start when unplaced over 1400m here. Rock hard fit and finds a nice race. DON'S PARTY (2) drops back in trip after a modest effort last time out at Newcastle. Top four contender.",
